  "dimensions": [
    {
      "dimension":"scope",
      "explanation":"The stated actors are distributors. Promotion to a client covers both specific products and particular product types, including certain fund types and fund houses. The selected application remains within the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund context.",
      "source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"definitions",
      "explanation":"Neither gift nor discount is exhaustively defined. Additional returns and incentives may be gifts; that classification is not automatic. Actual fund return and distributor top-up return are expressly distinguished.",
      "source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],
      "status":"AMBIGUOUS"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"exceptions",
      "explanation":"The parenthetical exception attaches to discounts of fees or charges. A separately identifiable discount does not expressly exempt another benefit in a combined offer. Whether a fee-linked rebate actually qualifies as a discount remains unresolved.",
      "source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"modality",
      "explanation":"The selected standard says should not offer. The proposed compliance predicate models conformity to that stated standard without converting it into the separate statutory offence. May be considered preserves judgment over classification.",
      "source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"time",
      "explanation":"The restriction concerns offering gifts during promotion. No effective date, transition period or payment deadline is supplied. The FAQ’s 30 September 2010 date identifies a source, not a commencement date.",
      "source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"dependencies",
      "explanation":"The gift control is independently relevant even when an arrangement is not a structured product. The Code and supporting FAQ are identified but not supplied in full; section 103 authorisation or exemption does not establish satisfaction of the gift control.",
      "source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u28.7987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What distinguishes a genuine discount of fees or charges from a cash incentive calculated by reference to fees, particularly where payment is conditional on continued investment?",
    "What criteria in the referenced Code and FAQ determine gift classification and linkage to a particular product type?",
    "For a combined offer, which benefits are independently identifiable, and which form a single economically inseparable benefit?"
  ],
  "readings": [
    {
      "assumptions": [
        "The selected control assesses one identified benefit offered by one distributor in the SFC-authorised-fund context.",
        "Separately identifiable benefits in a combined offer are assessed separately; identifying those benefits may require judgment.",
        "Gift classification, discount classification and promotional linkage are supplied judgments, not inferred from a benefit’s label or from the mere existence of additional returns.",
        "The result is interpreted only when scope is true; unknown facts remain unknown."
      ],
      "citations": [
        {
          "quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)",
          "unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"
        },
        {
          "quote":"(i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.",
          "unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"
        },
        {
          "quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO",
          "unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"
        },
        {
          "quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.",
          "unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"
        },
        {
          "quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.",
          "unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"
        },
        {
          "quote":"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses",
          "unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"
        },
        {
          "quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.",
          "unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"
        }
      ],
      "distinction":"The discount exception applies to the identified benefit, while product-type promotion remains covered. For example, an offer promoting funds of one fund house could combine a fee reduction with a separately identifiable shopping voucher. Assuming the voucher is a gift and not a fee discount, the fee reduction satisfies this control and the voucher fails it. The text does not support exempting the entire package because one component is a discount, or excluding it because no individual fund is singled out. A fee-linked cash rebate presents a genuine unresolved classification question: if it is a discount it satisfies this control; if it is a non-discount gift it fails. The packet does not supply enough criteria to choose between those classifications.",
